+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Orders are long-lived support records, but deleting a customer currently makes those records inaccessible through the admin order APIs. The admin order list also loses all results after its first page, preventing support staff from finding older orders.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Preserve the customer identifier and order-time billing, delivery, and email details needed to read an order after its customer account is deleted.
+- Allow an admin to open, update the status of, and read history and payment transactions for an order whose customer no longer exists.
+- Make customer-order lookup use the order’s stored customer id rather than requiring a current customer record; return an empty result for ids with no orders.
+- Correct admin order-list paging, filtering, newest-first ordering, `recordsTotal`, and `totalPages` for all pages, including empty pages after the last page.
+- Keep re-registration with a deleted email independent from the deleted account’s historical orders.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `order-record-retention`: Retain and administer historical orders independently of the customer account lifecycle.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- Admin order API endpoints under `/api/v1/private/orders`.
+- Order/customer lookup and order criteria pagination in `sm-shop` and `sm-core`.
+- API/service tests covering deleted customers, filters, page totals, ordering, and account re-registration.
