+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Keeps historical order records available to support staff after a customer account is deleted, while preserving account isolation when an email address is later registered again.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Historical orders remain readable after account deletion
+The system SHALL retain an order’s stored customer id, order-time email, billing details, delivery details, status, history, and payment transactions independently of the current customer account.
+
+#### Scenario: Open an order after its customer is deleted
+- **WHEN** an administrator requests `GET /api/v1/private/orders/{id}` for an order whose customer account no longer exists
+- **THEN** the response is successful, includes the stored billing, delivery, and placement-email details, and has no current customer object
+
+#### Scenario: Administer a deleted-customer order
+- **WHEN** an administrator changes the status or reads history or payment transactions for an order whose customer account was deleted
+- **THEN** the operation succeeds using the order record and its related history or transactions
+
+### Requirement: Customer order lookup is independent of account existence
+The system SHALL list every order carrying the requested customer id, newest first, regardless of whether a customer record currently exists.
+
+#### Scenario: List orders for a deleted customer id
+- **WHEN** an administrator requests `GET /api/v1/private/orders/customers/{id}` after that customer account has been deleted
+- **THEN** the response contains all matching historical orders in newest-first order and `recordsTotal` equals the number of matching orders
+
+#### Scenario: List orders for an id with no orders
+- **WHEN** an administrator requests customer-order lookup for an id with no matching orders
+- **THEN** the response is successful with an empty order list and `recordsTotal` equal to `0`
+
+### Requirement: Admin order pagination reports complete filtered results
+The system SHALL return the requested zero-based page of orders matching status, email, name, and id filters, ordered newest first, with `recordsTotal` equal to the total matching orders and `totalPages` equal to the number of pages for the requested count.
+
+#### Scenario: Retrieve a later page
+- **WHEN** an administrator requests `GET /api/v1/private/orders?count=n&page=p` with a page within the filtered result set
+- **THEN** the response contains page `p` and retains the complete matching `recordsTotal` and calculated `totalPages`
+
+#### Scenario: Retrieve a page after the last page
+- **WHEN** an administrator requests a page beyond the last matching page
+- **THEN** the response contains no orders while retaining the same `recordsTotal` and `totalPages` as an in-range request
+
+### Requirement: Re-registered email accounts are separate identities
+The system SHALL associate newly registered accounts with a new customer id and SHALL NOT expose historical orders belonging to a deleted customer id through the new account.
+
+#### Scenario: Register again after deletion
+- **WHEN** a customer registers a new account using the email address from a deleted account
+- **THEN** the new account is created separately and its authenticated order view contains none of the deleted account’s historical orders
