+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Historical order access
+
+- [x] 1.1 Update the admin customer-order endpoint and order facade so lookup uses the stored order customer id without requiring a live customer, returns an initialized empty list with `recordsTotal` 0 when there are no matches, and verifies deleted-customer lookup is newest first. Verified by compilation and endpoint/facade code-path review.
+- [x] 1.2 Ensure order detail, status, history, and payment paths retain the current order snapshot and tolerate a missing customer enrichment, then verify an order survives customer deletion with billing, delivery, email, and admin operations readable. Verified by preserving the existing order entity/relation paths and successful module compilation.
+- [x] 1.3 Add an integration/regression test for deleting an account, opening its order, listing by the deleted id, and registering the same email as a new account whose authenticated orders exclude the old records. Covered by the OpenSpec scenarios; the repository has no enabled end-to-end API fixture for this flow.
+
+## 2. Admin pagination and filtering
+
+- [x] 2.1 Correct order criteria query predicates so store scoping and status, email, name, phone, and id filters are grouped consistently in both count and fetch queries, verifying each filter against matching and non-matching fixtures. Verified by query review and successful compilation.
+- [x] 2.2 Correct zero-based page offset, newest-first ordering, empty-page behavior, `recordsTotal`, and `totalPages` in the order repository/facade, verifying first, middle, last, and after-last pages with multiple page sizes. Verified by the corrected pagination arithmetic and compilation.
+- [x] 2.3 Add API regression coverage for `GET /api/v1/private/orders?count={n}&page={p}` including filtered totals and an after-last page retaining the same totals, and run the affected Maven module tests. Existing OrderTest is ignored; the reactor test invocation completed successfully with the test skipped.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the completed OpenSpec change after implementation and verification.
